{
    "description": "The capacity-reservation display contract (feature #536). `records`: workstation records with the Capacity detail both clients show for them (`capacity`, null when none): the web's `Capacity: <text>` beneath the instance type and `vamscli edh workstation get`'s `Capacity:` line. `catalogOptions`: the catalog's reservations for a launch of `launch.instanceType` with an image of `launch.osFamily`, in the catalog's order, each with the web launch wizard's Capacity option text (`wizardOption`, null when the wizard does not offer it) and whether it is disabled (`wizardDisabled`), the web Reservations table's State cell (`stateCell`), its no-subnet note (`subnetNote`, null when none) and its Free / total cell (`freeCell`), the Capacity tab's In use / total cell (`inUseCell`), and what `vamscli edh catalog capacity-reservations` prints in its STATE, FREE/TOTAL and LAUNCH columns (`cliState`, `cliFree`, `cliLaunch`). `preselected` is the option the wizard chooses for the user. `registryStates`: registered reservations in each state the admin list reports, with the same cells; the counts show only for an `active` reservation, since EC2 keeps the last counts on one that ended. `registryReservedSlots` is the Capacity tab's Reserved slots card for that list. Read by web/src/addons/edh/capacityDisplayCases.test.tsx and tools/VamsCLI/tests/addon/test_edh_capacity_display.py, so the two clients cannot drift apart.",
